{
    "_comment": [
        "Performance baseline for tests/backend_parity/test_performance_regression.cpp.",
        "HOST-KEYED map: { 'hosts': { '<hostname>': { 'ops': { '<op>_<size>':",
        "{ '<backend>': { 'median_ms': X, 'p99_ms': Y } } } } } }.",
        "Each host keeps its own block so a CI self-hosted runner and a developer",
        "laptop can both commit numbers without clobbering each other.",
        "",
        "Values are (re)generated per host by `python tools/regen_perf_baseline.py`,",
        "which rewrites ONLY the current host's entry (other hosts are preserved).",
        "",
        "Enforcement (EXPECT_LT) engages when TENZOR_PERF_ENFORCE=1 OR the running",
        "host (gethostname) has an entry under 'hosts' with a captured_at_iso8601",
        "no older than TENZOR_PERF_BASELINE_MAX_AGE_DAYS (default 90; a stale",
        "entry is treated the same as no entry at all -- see baseline_age_days()",
        "in test_performance_regression.cpp). Otherwise timings are printed and",
        "the check SKIPs with [MissingPerfBaseline].",
        "",
        "All 6 recorded op families are gated (MatMul/Conv2d at the tight",
        "tolerance; ElementwiseAdd/ReductionSum/Softmax/LayerNorm -- noisier,",
        "sub-millisecond ops -- at a separately-tunable, looser tolerance so",
        "ordinary OS/scheduler jitter on a shared host doesn't flake the gate).",
        "Tolerance (env-tunable):",
        "  TENZOR_PERF_REGRESSION_RTOL          \u2014 MatMul/Conv2d median (default 2.0).",
        "  TENZOR_PERF_REGRESSION_P99_RTOL      \u2014 MatMul/Conv2d p99    (default 3.0).",
        "  TENZOR_PERF_REGRESSION_FAST_OP_RTOL     \u2014 other 4 ops median (default 5.0).",
        "  TENZOR_PERF_REGRESSION_FAST_OP_P99_RTOL \u2014 other 4 ops p99    (default 8.0).",
        "",
        "Regenerate for each additional real host (CI runner + laptops) with",
        "`python tools/regen_perf_baseline.py --build-dir <dir>` so every op has",
        "values for that host too; only the running host's entry is rewritten."
    ],
